WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.292
BUKOLA AYODELE: Hi, I'm Bukola.

00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:03.330
And today, I'm super
excited to talk

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.810
about delivering high-performing
global APIs with Apigee

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:07.680
and Cloud CDN.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.872
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.150
With the power of digital, many
organizations across industries

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.990
are going global to unlock new
markets and optimize costs.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.870
As businesses expand
their global footprints,

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:30.320
they need to deliver connected
customer experiences,

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.900
integrate seamlessly
with regional partners,

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.920
and equip global
distributed workforces.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.870
APIs are packages of
data and functionality

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:43.490
that power digital experiences,
both customer-facing and

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.110
employee-facing.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.180
Therefore, as you
go global, it is

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.960
imperative to scale
your API programs.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.330
To help you globalize
your API initiatives,

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:56.630
Google Cloud brings together
Apigee and Cloud CDN,

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.570
the best of API management
and content delivery network

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.250
solutions.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.819
While Apigee builds a solid
foundation for your APIs,

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:08.270
Cloud CDN brings you the
same edge points of presence

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:12.020
that Google uses to serve its
web properties to billions

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.610
of users.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:17.330
By extending the power of
Cloud CDN to your APIs,

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:22.520
you can host your APIs across
24 regions in 73 zones,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.280
reduce the latency of
your APIs with caching

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.440
at more than a
hundred locations,

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:31.790
and increase the availability
for peak traffic seasons.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.960
Let's see a quick demo
of how this works.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.520
For the purpose
of this demo, I've

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.700
created a Hello
World API in Apigee.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.380
To protect this API, let's first
start by adding a Verify API

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.120
Key to this proxy.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.900
Once we do that, you'll see the
default is set to a queryparam,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.475
but let's change
this to a header.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:01.250
I'm now going to save
it as a new revision

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.730
and deploy it to the
demo environment.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:08.090
To consume this API, let's
create an API product

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.200
and add our API proxy to this
product by specifying the path.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.790
With this, the Hello World proxy
is now ready and accessible.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.880
Now let's see how to
apply Cloud CDN to improve

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:24.050
the caching of this API to
better serve global consumers.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:27.350
I created a very
simple Cloud CDN policy

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.720
and attached it to
a load balancer.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.480
I also pick the most basic
configuration for this policy.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.030
When I go to the
load balancer, you

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.120
can see that Cloud
CDN is enabled.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.170
I need to make one minor
addition to my API proxy

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:45.380
to let Cloud CDN know that
the response to this API

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.265
needs to be cached.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.560
When I access the
proxy from us-west,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.070
the call is executed in
about 10 milliseconds.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.990
If I take the same
call and execute it

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.830
from a VM located
in europe-west,

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.930
the response time for
this first attempt

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.660
is about 215 milliseconds.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.380
However, because of
enhanced caching,

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.240
the response time for
the second attempt

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.780
goes down to 16 milliseconds.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.670
That was just a
quick preview of how

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.700
to deliver high-performing
global APIs with Apigee

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.100
and Cloud CDN.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:29.330
In summary, Apigee and Cloud CDN
offer integrated out-of-the-box

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:33.020
capabilities to scale and
deliver high-performing APIs.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.910
Now it's your turn
to try it out and get

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.730
started by following the links
in the description box below.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:41.080
[MUSIC PLAYING]

